# A `.env` with an unterminated quote — the file interaction that only a
# WHOLE-FILE readback can see.
#
# `renderEnvValue` checks its candidate line in isolation, so a value carrying a
# `"` reads back as itself there and is written bare. Appended to this file, its
# quote CLOSES the one opened on the line below, and `resolve.ParseDotEnv` then
# reads A as everything up to it and never reaches the new name at all — the
# variable the compose file now references resolves to the empty string.
#
# Story 9.3 step 1's outer readback is the only thing that sees this. Delete it
# and both files are written.
A="unclosed
B=2
